Fix the Vercel production routing for the Admin frontend.

This is a Vite + React SPA using client-side routing.

When navigating inside the Admin Dashboard, routes work normally, but refreshing a nested route such as:

/dashboard
/collectors
/riders
/vehicles
/assignments
/collection-requests
/leaderboard
/reports

causes Vercel to return:

404 NOT_FOUND

Fix the frontend Vercel SPA routing so all React Router routes are served through the application's index.html.

Add or correctly update the Admin frontend vercel.json with the appropriate SPA rewrite:

{
  "rewrites": [
    {
      "source": "/(.*)",
      "destination": "/index.html"
    }
  ]
}

IMPORTANT:

This is ONLY for the Admin frontend Vercel deployment.

Do NOT modify the backend Vercel configuration.

Do NOT modify the API URL.

Do NOT modify authentication.

Do NOT modify QR functionality.

Do NOT modify Flutter/mobile functionality.

Do NOT modify the existing React routes.

Do NOT change unrelated application functionality.

After making the change:

1. Run the production build.
2. Verify the build succeeds.
3. Deploy the Admin frontend.
4. Test opening the Admin root URL.
5. Navigate to /dashboard.
6. Refresh /dashboard.
7. Navigate to /collectors and refresh.
8. Navigate to /riders and refresh.
9. Navigate to /vehicles and refresh.
10. Navigate to /assignments and refresh.
11. Navigate to /leaderboard and refresh.
12. Navigate to /reports and refresh.
13. Verify that every route loads instead of returning Vercel 404.
14. Verify API calls still use VITE_API_BASE_URL.

Do not make any unrelated changes.
